          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: Recent testimony (11/23/2009) of an old observation: in July 1979 (the witness cannot recall the exact date) two individuals experienced severe headaches after observing a bright flash on their bedroom wall. These headaches disappear simultaneously with the light phenomenon. Looking out the window to determine the source of the light, these two individuals observed several beams of light illuminating the road. The local newspaper later reported the presence of burned grass areas in a field in the area (no specifics on the local newspaper's name or the publication date of the article). No other testimony has been collected regarding this old observation, making any investigation difficult, if not impossible.",
